issue_context.body:
Currently the `CoarseFundamental.Price` property is `Raw` and this causes indicator problems with splits and dividends.

To solve the issue, we should add both price and split factors to the coarse fundamental `CSV` data files and in the `CoarseFundamental` class, so the adjusted price can be easily calculated.

These properties should be added to `CoarseFundamental`:
``` C#
        /// <summary>
        /// Gets the price factor for the given date
        /// </summary>
        public decimal PriceFactor { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// Gets the split factor for the given date
        /// </summary>
        public decimal SplitFactor { get; set; }

        /// <summary>
        /// Gets the combined factor used to create adjusted prices from raw prices
        /// </summary>
        public decimal PriceScaleFactor => PriceFactor * SplitFactor;

        /// <summary>
        /// Gets the split and dividend adjusted price
        /// </summary>
        public decimal AdjustedPrice => Price * PriceScaleFactor;
```

#### Reproducing the Problem
This is a simple daily universe algorithm with a price jump on the AAPL split:
``` C#
    public class BasicTemplateAlgorithm : QCAlgorithm
    {
        private static readonly Symbol Apple = QuantConnect.Symbol.Create("AAPL", SecurityType.Equity, Market.USA);

        public override void Initialize()
        {
            UniverseSettings.Resolution = Resolution.Daily;

            SetStartDate(2014, 06, 5);
            SetEndDate(2014, 06, 11);
            SetCash(50000);

            AddUniverse(coarse =>
            {
                var cf = coarse.FirstOrDefault(x => x.Symbol == Apple);
                if (cf != null)
                {
                    Console.WriteLine($"Symbol:{cf.Symbol.Value} EndTime:{cf.EndTime} RawPrice:{cf.Price}");
                }

                return new List<Symbol> {Apple};
            });
        }
    }
```

